.TH FETCH 1 "August 2026" "prebsd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fetch \- download a V6 or V7 disk image for prebsd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fetch
.RI [ name | all ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fetch
downloads and unpacks a Research Unix V6 or V7 disk image (or the V7 source
tape) named in the
.B images.tsv
manifest, into the current directory, so the per-image simh configs in
.BR ini/
can attach it.
With no argument it lists the available images.
With
.B all
it fetches every image.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B images.tsv
the manifest of images (name, URL, simh config, boot sequence, flags).
.TP
.BR ini/*.ini
one simh config per image.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boot.py (1)
